"# AGENTS.md

Instructions for coding agents working in this repo. Describe the project, its layout and its conventions here, outside the firescale block.

<!-- BEGIN firescale: written by \`fscale sync\` from \`fscale facts\`. Edits inside this block are replaced; write your own notes outside it. -->
## Commands

No build, lint, typecheck or test commands were found yet. Add them (for example as package scripts), then run \`fscale sync\` to list them here.

## Definition of done

Before you say a task is done, run \`npx firescale verify\` from the repo root and fix what it reports. It runs the firescale rules, then lint, typecheck and tests.

- Never skip, delete or weaken a test, a lint rule or a check to make it pass.
- \`SETUP NEEDED\` means the machine is not ready: a dependency, a program or a service is missing. Run the setup command it names, or tell the user. Do not change code for it. \`npx firescale doctor\` lists what is missing.
- To learn how to fix a rule's finding: \`npx firescale explain <rule>\`.
<!-- END firescale -->
"
`;
